flowchart LR
  accTitle: Evidence chain from stored memory to assessed outcome
  accDescr: A stable memory record can produce an access event. Only some retrieved memories are included in a prompt. Actual model use requires separate evidence, and causal contribution to an outcome requires attribution or controlled evaluation. These are not interchangeable events.
  M[(MemoryRecord)] --> A[MemoryAccessEvent]
  A -->|candidate retrieved| P[PromptInclusionEvent]
  A -->|miss, threshold fail, or rejected| R[Rejected candidate record]
  P -->|included| C[Prompt with memory version and position]
  P -->|not included| N[Inclusion rejection reason]
  C --> U{Evidence of actual use?}
  U -->|not observed| UN[Use unknown]
  U -->|observed| UE[Use evidence and trace]
  UE --> O[MemoryOutcomeEvent]
  UN --> O
  O --> AT[OutcomeMemoryAttribution]
  AT --> EV[Estimate contribution with uncertainty]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class M source
  class A,P,C,O,AT process
  class UE,EV output
  class R,N,U,UN caution
